# Current handoff

## Worldwide legal corpus objective — 2026-11-21

The current objective is autoformalization of the entire world legal corpus into source-grounded LegalIR and a versioned, compositional Lean4 corpus. The U.S. Code and Title 10 work remain pilots and benchmarks within that objective; their historical identities and results are preserved.

Parallel work uses existing owners for world/country-law source intake and Unicode spans (LIR-02/03), multilingual canonical matching and complete typed semantics (LIR-07), Lean interpretation/preservation/builds (LIR-12/13/14), learned retrieval/decoding (LIR-17/19/20), and per-jurisdiction coverage/dependency-component expansion (LIR-23/24). Source language, jurisdiction, instrument identity, governing edition, effectivity and definition dependencies must survive the translation. Dataset revision and successful compilation do not supply missing legal meaning.

Prioritize tasks that directly advance that pipeline. This scope correction changes no task states, historical experiment cutoffs or measured results, and reports no newly formalized law, legal review, model convergence or Lean build. All numerical observations below retain their original populations and dates.


